#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124320 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "266a9a4e-cb11-5e4a-a2ac-c2e734966372" :question/math-academy-id "e-5424" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4 \\times 4$ matrix, and \n![](images/6a/6a294de4a5f2ff5755d8ceb5b91bb8920685a1cf2b5e727c5b5fdcfaaf0b89b0.svg)\n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\textrm{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^4$\n\nIII. $\\textrm{rank}(A)=4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4 \\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following: \n\n![](images/4b/4b42fd4ec8ccf491a1244a648af6fe40ce846fad388685e36d499783a095f8f7.svg)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since \n![](images/32/327a582d15b82ebccda48358062310e6ad5c3bb2689f2024d76a8f8e7e1401a0.svg)\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1 \\neq 0.\n$$\n\nSo,  according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since the matrix $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\textrm{Col}(A) \\neq \\mathbb{R}^4.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\textrm{rank}(A) \\neq 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124433 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "c1120305-c8cb-5f57-97b1-9b31dc059b4a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9961" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\det(A) = 0$\n\nII. $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible ![](images/dc/dc72aea1969143a926fd637d3360bb42116b27545a748923069f4ae732bd700f.svg)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\det(A) = 0.$* $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\nSince $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ must be invertible, which means $\\det(A) \\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n.$* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=n,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124434 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "fff1daf8-5a1f-54c9-90d7-87710ca00d23" :question/math-academy-id "e-9962" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3e58a5f09c9060932ee854feeec0733dc9432c2de658308e3ebdccdd0ef89e5f.svg)\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. What should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n![](images/21/21455a41af5743da6f9f4de5e267c17c6037b929a01ba894cfd91530dbb39986.svg)\n\nThe missing expression is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A)).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8cade90-de90-5cc5-a96f-4b62957e1afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121332} {:answer/id #uuid "6b1a034d-0611-5f21-a47f-fb41d7d10986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121335} {:answer/id #uuid "72b6d84b-4599-5ae1-87e9-228fcb3fc5f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426052} {:answer/id #uuid "ad86e99c-d63c-534c-8616-6b38f0564843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426060} {:answer/id #uuid "c784e28a-945a-50b9-a3c3-88323f6f5bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad86e99c-d63c-534c-8616-6b38f0564843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426060} :answer-field/id #uuid "36cf5fde-aae3-5ac2-808d-cd031ad46138" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b33961fd-1191-51c9-841c-0bdd04b0318b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140766" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\{0\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36811030-e48f-580b-b28d-88329ce34cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426042} {:answer/id #uuid "5cde84ae-1075-5dc9-aebf-b837df68734b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426048} {:answer/id #uuid "8dce4f53-2c64-500a-bb6e-394ac019d1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{n}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426055} {:answer/id #uuid "9a1230e7-e926-5f64-a23e-9a6e2909fa72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426058} {:answer/id #uuid "ab023700-fa22-514b-bf5f-5062513b1047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36811030-e48f-580b-b28d-88329ce34cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426042} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bb630b8-37fa-5f0a-a193-e8a8a792e3e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "937a6bb1-f955-5ee0-bbd6-d97686bceb6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142471" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=\\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}}=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "302eb5c9-529d-52e1-a2c8-d1933af5ef1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269702} {:answer/id #uuid "3248b20a-91c4-5f7a-8779-ea6de359ff74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269724} {:answer/id #uuid "50abda73-b0d4-5a29-bbed-94088d819a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269993} {:answer/id #uuid "81cab381-305e-5227-96c9-4247414173f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270391} {:answer/id #uuid "aa256175-82e0-56ad-9450-2d16ed6ca6ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "302eb5c9-529d-52e1-a2c8-d1933af5ef1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269702} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecf48405-f1ff-5682-8eff-4a48eebe4c60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4927fd87-c83e-52d3-b9bb-877110a8c514" :question/math-academy-id "q-142474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}?\n$$\n\n- $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n- $A$ is invertible\n- $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0895ab25-c3a3-5de5-8c7f-b29240d396fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269347} {:answer/id #uuid "70dbe989-e5af-54e0-b64e-b2b8f149ec2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270271} {:answer/id #uuid "8abda789-acc5-5411-8952-794fc73da646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270468} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e8d21b-4e62-5248-a3d7-8afaad5786f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270745} {:answer/id #uuid "be53ddb2-3789-59ea-8a22-87a097d55924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0895ab25-c3a3-5de5-8c7f-b29240d396fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269347} :answer-field/id #uuid "afe26b88-241f-530c-8ccf-982cdb7e7d4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7036dc73-9ca4-59f2-b983-11eaacfb5a4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142476" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $det(A)=0$\n- $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}$\n- $A$ has $8$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $  \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}.$*  $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $8$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=8,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $8$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097b8a1b-b44d-5e76-97c8-b4c1a59a0e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345426} {:answer/id #uuid "6baff456-609b-5210-afb9-ca38e5adabcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346284} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc14084-3088-5b8a-ba2d-7b0e0a1aadc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346981} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb60f3a-a601-548c-bc1f-20c9cc148f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347151} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc15575-a017-565f-8f76-b1cadb4fc7dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbc14084-3088-5b8a-ba2d-7b0e0a1aadc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346981} :answer-field/id #uuid "458244de-522e-5387-a418-9f5ed1cbeef6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e25ee2d5-6236-5cb7-ae46-36798fde6f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-79334" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $A$ is **not** invertible\n- $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n- $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,\\times $\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}]}
